  "subject": "mathematics",
  "summary": "A semester of Grade 7 mathematics: proportional relationships and percent, expressions and two-step equations and inequalities, operations with rational numbers, geometry (scale drawings, circles, angles, area, surface area and volume), probability, and statistics and sampling. Units are numbered 2 to 7 to match the Northfield showcase class; a district's own opening unit, such as a review of Grade 6 ratios and number skills, fits before them. Each unit has a student overview with a worked example, a teacher guide with a five-day plan, a lesson, problem-set assignments, an assessment with a rubric and an answer key.",
  "title": "Mathematics 7",
  "version": "1.0.0"
